# api.intelcost.io in front of the live api colour (D-842). The colour is one line in live/upstream.caddy, written by
# rollout.sh; `caddy reload` swaps it gracefully: requests in flight finish where they started, new ones go to the new
# colour, and WebSockets on the old one stay up to 5 minutes or until that colour stops (1012, then they reconnect).
# Realtime needs nothing else from Caddy (notes/2026-09-26_realtime_caddy_for_abdullah.md).
#
# No active health check here: a colour is sent traffic only once Docker reports it healthy (rollout.sh), and the api's
# /health asks the database, Redis and the bucket, too much to ask every few seconds under load (the bench's check: a
# 3 s probe timed out under it and Caddy answered 503 with the api up). A request that cannot reach the colour is
# tried again for up to 10 s, and a colour that fails is left out for 5 s.
{$API_SITE} {
	reverse_proxy {
		import /etc/caddy/live/upstream.caddy
		lb_try_duration 10s
		lb_try_interval 250ms
		fail_duration 5s
		max_fails 1
		stream_close_delay 5m
	}
}
